  "instruction": "Return ['option_id', 'lane', 'cost_cents', 'duration_minutes'] with types INTEGER,VARCHAR,INTEGER,INTEGER, option_id ascending. Each row is one unique option_id shipping proposal for a nonnull arbitrary text lane (empty text allowed). Cost is integer currency cents; duration is whole elapsed minutes. Both metrics are nullable and otherwise [0,2147483647]. Incomplete options (either metric NULL) are excluded as both candidates and competitors. Retain complete options unless some same-lane complete competitor has cost <= candidate cost AND duration <= candidate duration AND at least one strict improvement. Use a correlated NOT EXISTS subquery. Equal metric pairs do not dominate each other and all their distinct option_ids survive; no single-winner tie-break. Self cannot dominate itself. Output once per surviving option. Empty input or all incomplete options gives empty output. No date/status filter or missing-settlement history semantics.",
